                                                    ⚓⚓HRMS App - Folder Structure and Setup Guide:⚓⚓

🧱Step 1:Create the base structure
# Create root folder
mkdir hrms-app && cd hrms-app

# Initialize a workspace
npm init -y

# Create apps and packages folders
mkdir -p apps/frontend packages/ui packages/shared

# folder structure frontend :
hrms-app/
│
├── apps/
│   └── frontend-ui-monorepo/
│       ├── public/
│       ├── src/
│       │   ├── assets/                # images, icons
│       │   ├── components/            # shared components (Navbar, Sidebar, etc.)
│       │   ├── features/              # each module from flowchart
│       │   │   ├── home/
│       │   │   ├── employee/
│       │   │   ├── attendance/
│       │   │   ├── leaves/
│       │   │   ├── performance/
│       │   │   ├── payroll/
│       │   │   ├── settings/
│       │   ├── hooks/                 # custom React hooks
│       │   ├── layouts/               # page layouts (DashboardLayout, AuthLayout)
│       │   ├── pages/                 # route-level components (if using React Router)
│       │   ├── services/              # API calls (Axios / Fetch)
│       │   ├── store/                 # Redux or Zustand
│       │   ├── utils/                 # helper functions (formatDate, etc.)
│       │   ├── constants/             # role names, permissions, etc.
│       │   ├── App.jsx
│       │   └── main.jsx
│       ├── package.json
│       └── vite.config.js
│
├── packages/
│   ├── ui/                            # reusable UI components (for scalability)
│   ├── shared/                        # constants, types, validation logic shared across apps
│
├── turbo.json or nx.json              # monorepo config
├── package.json
└── README.md

🧱 Step 2: Setup the React Frontend (Vite):
cd apps
npm create vite@latest frontend -- --template react
cd frontend
npm install

🧱 Step 3: Organize folders inside src/
cd src
mkdir assets components features hooks layouts pages services store utils constants
cd features && mkdir home employee attendance leaves performance payroll settings

🧱 Step 4: Setup aliases and configs (clean imports)

In your vite.config.js, add this:
import { defineConfig } from 'vite'
import react from '@vitejs/plugin-react'
import path from 'path'

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react()],
  resolve: {
    alias: {
      '@': path.resolve(__dirname, './src'),
    },
  },
})

Now you can import like this:
e.g.import Navbar from '@/components/Navbar'
import { getEmployees } from '@/services/employee'

🧱 Step 5: Base Dependencies (recommended):
Inside apps/frontend, install:
npm install react-router-dom axios @reduxjs/toolkit react-redux
npm install @chakra-ui/react @emotion/react @emotion/styled framer-motion
npm install react-hook-form react-query

🧱 Step 6: Monorepo Setup  (root level):
At the root of hrms-app, modify your root package.json to look like:
{
  "name": "hrms-app",
  "private": true,
  "workspaces": [
    "apps/*",
    "packages/*"
  ]
}
If you want to use Turborepo for speed:
npm install turbo --save-dev

Then create turbo.json in the root:
{
  "$schema": "https://turbo.build/schema.json",
  "pipeline": {
    "dev": {
      "cache": false
    },
    "build": {
      "dependsOn": ["^build"],
      "outputs": ["dist/**"]
    }
  }
}

Now you can run frontend via:
cd hrms-app
npx turbo run dev --filter=frontend

🧱 Step 7: Optional Packages for Scalability (Later)

packages/ui/ → shared buttons, modals, etc.

packages/shared/ → constants, validations, hooks shared across frontend/backend later.

✅ Your folder structure is now ready:
hrms-app/
├── apps/
│   └── frontend-ui-monorepo/
│       ├── public/
│       ├── src/
│       │   ├── assets/
│       │   ├── components/
│       │   ├── features/
│       │   │   ├── employee/
│       │   │   ├── attendance/
│       │   │   ├── leaves/
│       │   │   ├── payroll/
│       │   │   ├── performance/
│       │   │   ├── settings/
│       │   │   └── home/
│       │   ├── hooks/
│       │   ├── layouts/
│       │   ├── pages/
│       │   ├── services/
│       │   ├── store/
│       │   ├── utils/
│       │   ├── constants/
│       │   ├── App.jsx
│       │   └── main.jsx
│       ├── package.json
│       └── vite.config.js
├── packages/
│   ├── ui/
│   └── shared/
├── package.json
└── turbo.json




